Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper alignment of the `device_addr4` opaque data in the `getdeviceinfo` reply, which resulted in insufficient space being allocated for the reply data, leading to potential data corruption or misinterpretation of the reply structure.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
replen = hdr.replen + op_decode_hdr_maxsz;
rpc_prepare_reply_pages(req, args->pdev->pages, args->pdev->pgbase,
                        args->pdev->pglen, hdr.replen - 2);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the calculation of `replen` does not account for the necessary padding for the `device_addr4` opaque data, leading to insufficient space being allocated in the reply pages. This misalignment can cause data corruption or misinterpretation of the reply structure.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
replen = hdr.replen + op_decode_hdr_maxsz;
rpc_prepare_reply_pages(req, args->pdev->pages, args->pdev->pgbase,
                        args->pdev->pglen, replen + 2 + 1);
```
Reason:
The fix adjusts the calculation of the size passed to `rpc_prepare_reply_pages` by including the correct padding for the `device_addr4` opaque data. This ensures that sufficient space is allocated for the reply data, preventing potential data corruption or misinterpretation.


Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:
		.minorversion = nfs4_xdr_minorversion(&args->seq_args),
	};

	encode_compound_hdr(xdr, req, &hdr);
	encode_sequence(xdr, &args->seq_args, &hdr);
	encode_getdeviceinfo(xdr, args, &hdr);

	/* set up reply kvec. Subtract notification bitmap max size (2)
	 * so that notification bitmap is put in xdr_buf tail */
	rpc_prepare_reply_pages(req, args->pdev->pages, args->pdev->pgbase,
				args->pdev->pglen, hdr.replen - 2);
	encode_nops(&hdr);
}

